From: W1700K port <w1700k@localhost>
Date: Sat, 23 Aug 2026 00:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: track direct bridge fallback lifetime

The PPE bridge-FDB fallback can bind an unbound FOE hash before the
netfilter flowtable installs an L2 master flow.  Its direct form did not
allocate a software subflow object, so nothing invalidated that hash when
the selected WLAN/GDM egress device went down or was unregistered.  SSID
or AP-interface reloads could therefore leave hardware entries pointing
at a stale BSS/WCID path.

Allocate a tracked subflow for direct binds, store the actual committed
hardware entry (not merely the bridge template), and keep a reference on
the resolved egress netdev.  Remove matching entries from GOING_DOWN,
DOWN and UNREGISTER events, and clean all direct entries during PPE exit.

Signed-off-by: W1700K port <w1700k@localhost>
